=== S4. New findings (both report only, not blocking)
F7. B10 passes the suite. The prompt names `camera.enable-all`; the pattern
reads `camera.enable`, which is in the vocabulary, and stops at the hyphen.
F8. B11 passes the suite. The prompt names `system.x`; a later part must
have two or more characters, so `system.x` is not seen. That rule is what
keeps "e.g." and "i.e." out, so it was a trade-off, not an oversight.

Both gaps are in the pattern the reviewer suggested in S5 above (F5+F6);
the author applied it as given. Why not blocking:
- The done-when holds: "W4 summary: 4 of 4 probes caught" (S2).
- The broker looks a name up by exact match (`CATALOGUE.get(name)`,
  capabilities.py line 152), and test_unknown_capability_is_denied
  (test_capabilities.py line 76) shows an unknown name is denied. A name the
  prompt invents is refused at the boundary; the prompt test is the alarm
  for drift, not the boundary.

A pattern that closes both, checked against the real prompt
(<scratch>/r10_f7f8.py, run 2026-10-16 from the repo root; it imports
SYSTEM_PROMPT and nothing from the test):
