'system.x'               current=[] candidate=['system.x']
'usb2.mount'             current=['usb2.mount'] candidate=['usb2.mount']
The candidate is
    \b[a-z][a-z0-9_]*(?:\.[a-z](?:[a-z0-9_-]*[a-z0-9_])?)+
with one more rule: keep a match only if at least one part is longer than
one letter. It finds the same seven names in the prompt, sees B7, B8, B10
and B11, and finds nothing in "e.g.", "i.e.", "a.m.", "1.2.3" or a
sentence-final period. This is a follow-up for the author, not a condition
of this verdict.

